; a numeric magnitude that has entered the question graph but is not yet
; bound to any rashi. held provisionally until sankhya-bandha attaches it
; to the preceding active rashi.
; 
; example: "ball has mass 5 kg"
; before binding: [5, asprista-sankhya, 5.0]  — the 5 is floating
; after binding:  [mass, sankhya, 5.0]        — the 5 belongs to mass's rashi
; 
; asprista = not yet touched by understanding (which rashi does this belong to?)
; sankhya  = numeric magnitude
; together: a magnitude whose rashi owner has not yet been discerned
; 
; resolves into sankhya on binding. remains asprista-sankhya if no rashi precedes it.

(sangati asprista-sankhya
  (sthita prashna asprista sankhya mithya-satya))
